#: ../../getting_started/installation/overview.rst:4
msgid "Installation Overview"
msgstr "Descripción general de la instalación"

#: ../../getting_started/installation/overview.rst:6
msgid ""
"|morpheus| supports two primary deployment methods. Choose the path that "
"fits your environment:"
msgstr "|morpheus| admite dos métodos de implementación principales. Elija la ruta que se adapte a su entorno:"

#: ../../getting_started/installation/overview.rst:11
msgid "HPE HVM Deployment (Recommended)"
msgstr "Implementación HPE HVM (recomendada)"

#: ../../getting_started/installation/overview.rst:13
msgid ""
"For customers using HPE HVM as their hypervisor platform, |morpheus| is "
"deployed as a virtual appliance directly onto an HVM host using the **HPE"
" Morpheus Manager Installer**. This is the fastest and simplest path to a"
" running |morpheus| environment. This approach:"
msgstr "Para clientes que utilizan HPE HVM como plataforma de hipervisor, |morpheus| se implementa como un dispositivo virtual directamente en un host HVM usando el **HPE Morpheus Manager Installer**. Esta es la ruta más rápida y sencilla hacia un entorno |morpheus| en ejecución. Este enfoque:"

#: ../../getting_started/installation/overview.rst:15
msgid "Takes **15–30 minutes** from start to a running appliance"
msgstr "Toma **15–30 minutos** desde el inicio hasta un dispositivo en ejecución"

#: ../../getting_started/installation/overview.rst:16
msgid ""
"Requires no manual package installation — the installer handles image "
"upload, VM creation, and configuration"
msgstr "No requiere instalación manual de paquetes — el instalador gestiona la carga de imagen, creación de VM y configuración"

#: ../../getting_started/installation/overview.rst:17
msgid "Deploys a fully self-contained appliance from a QCOW2 image"
msgstr "Implementa un dispositivo completamente autocontenido desde una imagen QCOW2"

#: ../../getting_started/installation/overview.rst:18
msgid ""
"Can deploy a local QCOW2 image entirely over the local network without "
"internet access"
msgstr "Puede implementar una imagen QCOW2 local completamente a través de la red local sin acceso a internet"

#: ../../getting_started/installation/overview.rst:20
msgid "**To get started with HVM deployment:**"
msgstr "**Para comenzar con la implementación HVM:**"

#: ../../getting_started/installation/overview.rst:22
msgid ""
":doc:`Prepare your HVM host(s) "
"</getting_started/installation/hvm_host_prep>` — Install HVM OS 24.04 on "
"bare-metal servers and configure networking. This is required before "
"running the installer."
msgstr ":doc:`Prepare sus host(s) HVM </getting_started/installation/hvm_host_prep>` — Instale HVM OS 24.04 en servidores bare-metal y configure la red. Esto es necesario antes de ejecutar el instalador."

#: ../../getting_started/installation/overview.rst:23
msgid ""
":doc:`Deploy Morpheus with the HPE Installer "
"</getting_started/installation/singleNode/hpe_installer>` — Run the "
"graphical installer from your workstation to deploy the |morpheus| "
"appliance VM onto a prepared HVM host."
msgstr ":doc:`Implemente Morpheus con el HPE Installer </getting_started/installation/singleNode/hpe_installer>` — Ejecute el instalador gráfico desde su estación de trabajo para implementar la VM del dispositivo |morpheus| en un host HVM preparado."

#: ../../getting_started/installation/overview.rst:25
msgid ""
"After the appliance is running, you can add additional HVM hosts to form "
"a cluster from within the |morpheus| UI (:menuselection:`Infrastructure "
"--> Clusters`)."
msgstr "Después de que el dispositivo esté en ejecución, puede agregar hosts HVM adicionales para formar un clúster desde la UI de |morpheus| (:menuselection:`Infrastructure --> Clusters`)."

#: ../../getting_started/installation/overview.rst:27
msgid ""
"Local deployment and ongoing maintenance have different connectivity "
"requirements. The Manager's Ubuntu base OS still requires an HPE-approved"
" APT source for security and package updates. For connected and air-"
"gapped options, see :doc:`Morpheus Manager Base OS Updates "
"</getting_started/maintenance/manager_os_updates>`."
msgstr "La implementación local y el mantenimiento continuo tienen requisitos de conectividad diferentes. El SO base Ubuntu del Manager aún requiere una fuente APT aprobada por HPE para actualizaciones de seguridad y paquetes. Para opciones conectadas y air-gapped, consulte :doc:`Morpheus Manager Base OS Updates </getting_started/maintenance/manager_os_updates>`."

#: ../../getting_started/installation/overview.rst:32
msgid "Manual Package Installation"
msgstr "Instalación manual de paquetes"

#: ../../getting_started/installation/overview.rst:34
msgid ""
"For environments that do **not** use HPE HVM — such as existing VMware, "
"Hyper-V, cloud VMs, or bare-metal Linux servers — |morpheus| is available"
" as standard ``debian`` or ``yum`` packages installed directly on a "
"supported Linux OS. This method is also used for advanced deployment "
"topologies (distributed services, full HA) where you need granular "
"control over each component."
msgstr "Para entornos que **no** utilizan HPE HVM — como VMware existente, Hyper-V, VMs en la nube o servidores Linux bare-metal — |morpheus| está disponible como paquetes estándar ``debian`` o ``yum`` instalados directamente en un SO Linux compatible. Este método también se utiliza para topologías de implementación avanzadas (servicios distribuidos, HA completa) donde necesita control granular sobre cada componente."

#: ../../getting_started/installation/overview.rst:36
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The default configuration installs all required services on a single "
"host. |morpheus| can also be configured in a distributed architecture "
"with external services and multiple application hosts for High "
"Availability."
msgstr ""
"|morpheus| viene empaquetado como un paquete basado en ``debian`` o "
"``yum``. La configuración predeterminada instala todos los servicios "
"requeridos en una sola vm o Host bare metal. Morpheus puede configurarse "
"en una arquitectura distribuida para usar uno o múltiples servicios "
"externos, y múltiples Hosts de aplicación pueden configurarse para "
"configuraciones de Alta disponibilidad."

#: ../../getting_started/installation/overview.rst:38
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"All components are installed and configured during the ``morpheus-ctl "
"reconfigure`` command. The config file ``/etc/morpheus/morpheus.rb`` can "
"optionally point the application to external services (distributed "
"configuration)."
msgstr ""
"Todos los componentes requeridos para Morpheus se instalan y configuran "
"por defecto durante el comando ``reconfigure`` de Morpheus. El archivo de"
" configuración de Morpheus, ``morpheus.rb``, puede configurarse "
"opcionalmente para apuntar la aplicación Morpheus a servicios externos "
"(configuración distribuida)."

#: ../../getting_started/installation/overview.rst:40
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"|morpheus| Release Packages can be obtained from `HPE My Software Center "
"<https://myenterpriselicense.hpe.com/>`_."
msgstr ""
"Las URLs de paquetes de versiones de |morpheus| pueden obtenerse en "
"`https://app.morpheushub.com <https://app.morpheushub.com>`_"

#: ../../getting_started/installation/overview.rst:42
msgid "Important"
msgstr "Importante"

#: ../../getting_started/installation/overview.rst:42
msgid ""
"|morpheus| requires TLS v1.2 for all incoming appliance connections. "
"Ensure front-end load balancers and agents support TLS v1.2 or higher."
msgstr "|morpheus| requiere TLS v1.2 para todas las conexiones entrantes al dispositivo. Asegúrese de que los balanceadores de carga front-end y los agentes admitan TLS v1.2 o superior."

#: ../../getting_started/installation/overview.rst:45
msgid "Architecture Options"
msgstr "Opciones de arquitectura"

#: ../../getting_started/installation/overview.rst:47
msgid "Single Host (All-In-One/default)"
msgstr "Host único (Todo-en-uno/predeterminado)"

#: ../../getting_started/installation/overview.rst:48
msgid ""
"All tiers running on a single host. The reconfigure process installs all "
"required services. This is the default configuration."
msgstr ""
"Todas las capas ejecutándose en un solo host. El proceso de "
"reconfiguración instala todos los servicios requeridos. Esta es la "
"configuración predeterminada."

#: ../../getting_started/installation/overview.rst:49
#: ../../getting_started/installation/overview.rst:101
msgid "Single Hosts with Distributed Service(s)"
msgstr "Host único con servicio(s) distribuido(s)"

#: ../../getting_started/installation/overview.rst:50
msgid ""
"Transactional Database, Non-Transactional Database, and/or Message tiers "
"are externalized, with the remaining services on a single host. The "
"reconfigure process installs all services not set to false in "
"``/etc/morpheus/morpheus.rb``"
msgstr ""
"Las capas de Base de datos transaccional, Base de datos no transaccional "
"y/o Mensajería se externalizan, con los servicios restantes en un solo "
"host. El proceso de reconfiguración instala todos los servicios que no "
"estén configurados como false en ``/etc/morpheus/morpheus.rb``"

#: ../../getting_started/installation/overview.rst:51
msgid "Clustered Hosts with Distributed Transactional Database (3-Node HA)"
msgstr ""
"Hosts en clúster con base de datos transaccional distribuida (Alta "
"disponibilidad de 3 nodos)"

#: ../../getting_started/installation/overview.rst:52
msgid ""
"Application, Message, and Non-Transactional tiers are installed and "
"clustered on three or more application hosts. The Transactional Database "
"Tier remains outside the application hosts, and every application host is"
" configured to use the same external MySQL cluster or supported service. "
"Reconfigure does not install MySQL on the application hosts in this "
"topology."
msgstr "Los niveles Application, Message y Non-Transactional se instalan y agrupan en tres o más hosts de aplicación. El nivel Transactional Database Tier permanece fuera de los hosts de aplicación, y cada host de aplicación está configurado para usar el mismo clúster MySQL externo o servicio compatible. Reconfigure no instala MySQL en los hosts de aplicación en esta topología."

#: ../../getting_started/installation/overview.rst:53
msgid "App Host(s) with Distributed Services (Full HA)"
msgstr ""
"Host(s) de aplicación con servicios distribuidos (Alta disponibilidad "
"completa)"

#: ../../getting_started/installation/overview.rst:54
msgid ""
"Application tier is installed on one or more hosts. All UI hosts point to"
" externalized Transactional Database, Non-Transactional Database, and "
"Message Tiers. The reconfigure process installs only Application "
"services."
msgstr ""
"La capa de aplicación se instala en uno o más hosts. Todos los hosts de "
"UI apuntan a las capas externalizadas de Base de datos transaccional, "
"Base de datos no transaccional y Mensajería. El proceso de "
"reconfiguración instala solo los servicios de aplicación."

#: ../../getting_started/installation/overview.rst:57
msgid "Distributed Configurations"
msgstr "Configuraciones distribuidas"

#: ../../getting_started/installation/overview.rst:59
msgid ""
"Morpheus provides a wide array of options when it comes to deployment "
"architectures. It can start as a simple one machine instance where all "
"services run on the same machine, or it can be split off into individual "
"services per machine and configured in a high availability configuration,"
" either in the same region or cross-region. Naturally, high availability "
"can grow more complicated, depending on the configuration you want to do "
"and this article will cover the basic concepts of the Morpheus HA "
"architecture that can be used in a wide array of configurations."
msgstr ""
"Morpheus proporciona una amplia variedad de opciones en cuanto a "
"arquitecturas de despliegue. It can start as a simple one machine "
"instance where todos los servicios run on the mismo machine, o it puede "
"ser split off en individual services per machine y configurado in a high "
"availability configuration, ya sea in the mismo region o cross-region. "
"Naturally, high availability can grow more complicated, dependiendo de la"
" configuración you want to do y this article will cover the basic "
"concepts of the Morpheus HA architecture that puede usarse in una amplia "
"variedad de configurations."

#: ../../getting_started/installation/overview.rst:61
msgid ""
"There are four primary tiers of services represented within the Morpheus "
"appliance. They are the Application Tier, Transactional Database Tier, "
"Non-Transactional Database Tier, and Message Tier. Each of these tiers "
"have their own recommendations for High availability deployments that we "
"need to cover."
msgstr ""
"There are four primary tiers of services represented dentro de the "
"Morpheus appliance. They are the Application Tier, Transactional Database"
" Tier, Non-Transactional Database Tier, y Message Tier. Each de lase "
"tiers have their own recommendations for High availability deployments "
"that we need to cover."

#: ../../getting_started/installation/overview.rst:64
msgid "Application Tier"
msgstr "Capa de aplicación"

#: ../../getting_started/installation/overview.rst:65
msgid ""
"The application tier is easily installed with the same Debian or yum "
"repository package that Morpheus is normally distributed with. Advanced "
"configuration allows for the additional tiers to be skipped and leave "
"only the “stateless” services that need run. These stateless services "
"include Nginx and Tomcat. These machines should also have at least 8gb of"
" Memory. They can be configured across all regions and placed behind a "
"central load-balancer or Geo based load-balancer. They typically connect "
"to all other tiers as none of the other tiers talk to each other besides "
"through the central application tier. One final piece when it comes to "
"setting up the Application tier is a shared storage means is necessary "
"when it comes to maintaining things like deployment archives, virtual "
"image catalogs, backups, etc. These can be externalized to an object "
"storage service such as Amazon S3 or Openstack Swiftstack as well. If not"
" using those options a simple NFS cluster can also be used to handle the "
"shared storage structure."
msgstr ""
"The application tier is easily instalado con the mismo Debian o yum "
"repository package that Morpheus is normally distributed with. Advanced "
"configuration allows for the adicional tiers to be skipped y leave solo "
"the “stateless” services that need run. These stateless services include "
"Nginx y Tomcat. These machines should también have al menos 8gb of "
"Memory. They puede configurarse across todos regions y placed behind a "
"central load-balancer o Geo based load-balancer. They typically connect "
"to todos otros tiers as none of the otros tiers talk to cada otros "
"besides a través de the central application tier. One final piece when it"
" comes to setting up the Application tier is a shared storage means is "
"necessary when it comes to maintaining things like deployment archives, "
"virtual image catalogs, backups, etc. These puede ser externalized to an "
"object storage service como Amazon S3 o Openstack Swiftstack as well. If "
"no using those options a simple NFS cluster can también be used to handle"
" the shared storage structure."

#: ../../getting_started/installation/overview.rst:68
msgid "Transactional Database Tier"
msgstr "Capa de base de datos transaccional"

#: ../../getting_started/installation/overview.rst:69
msgid ""
"The Transactional database tier usually consists of a MySQL-compatible "
"database. It is recommended that a lockable clustered configuration be "
"used. There are several documents online related to configuring and "
"setting up such a cluster but it most simply can be laid out in a many-"
"master configuration. There can be some nodes setup with replication "
"delay as well as some with no replication delay. It is common practice to"
" have no replication delay within the same region and allow some "
"replication delay cross region. This does increase the risk of job run "
"overlap between the 2 regions however, the concurrent operations "
"typically self-correct and this is a non-issue."
msgstr ""
"The Transactional database tier usually consists of a MySQL-compatible "
"database. It se recomienda that a lockable clustered configuration be "
"used. There are several documents online relacionado con configuring y "
"setting up such a cluster pero it la mayoría de simply puede ser laid out"
" in a many-master configuration. There puede ser algunos nodes setup con "
"replication delay así como algunos con no replication delay. It is common"
" practice to have no replication delay dentro de the mismo region y allow"
" algunos replication delay cross region. This does increase the risk of "
"job run overlap entre the 2 regions sin embargo, the concurrent "
"operations typically self-correct y this is a non-issue."

#: ../../getting_started/installation/overview.rst:72
msgid "Non-Transactional Database Tier"
msgstr "Capa de base de datos no transaccional"

#: ../../getting_started/installation/overview.rst:73
msgid ""
"The Non-Transactional tier consists of an ElasticSearch (version 7.6.0) "
"cluster. Elastic Search is used for log aggregation data and temporal "
"aggregation data (essentially stats, metrics, and logs). This enables for"
" a high write throughput at scale. ElasticSearch is a Clustered database "
"meaning all nodes no matter the region need to be connected to each other"
" over what they call a “Transport” protocol. It is fairly simple to get "
"setup as all nodes are identical. It is also a Java-based system and does"
" require a sizable chunk of memory for larger data sets. 8 GB is "
"recommended and more nodes can be added to scale either horizontally or "
"vertically."
msgstr ""
"The Non-Transactional tier consists of an ElasticSearch (version 7.6.0) "
"cluster. Elastic Search is used for log aggregation data y temporal "
"aggregation data (essentially stats, metrics, y logs). This enables for a"
" high write throughput at scale. ElasticSearch is a Clustered database "
"meaning all nodes no matter the region necesitan ser connected to each "
"other over when lay call a “Transport” protocol. It is fairly simple to "
"get setup as all nodes are identical. It is también a Java-based system y"
" does require a sizable chunk of memory for larger data sets. 8 GB se "
"recomienda y more nodes puede ser added to scale either horizontally o "
"vertically."

#: ../../getting_started/installation/overview.rst:76
msgid "Messaging Tier"
msgstr "Capa de mensajería"

#: ../../getting_started/installation/overview.rst:77
msgid ""
"The Messaging tier is an AMQP based tier along with STOMP Protocol (used "
"for agent communication). The primary model recommended is to use "
"RabbitMQ for queue services. RabbitMQ is also a cluster-based queuing "
"system and needs at least 3 instances for HA configurations. This is due "
"to elections in the failover scenarios RabbitMQ can manage. If doing a "
"cross-region HA RabbitMQ cluster, it is recommended to have at least 3 "
"Rabbit queue clusters per region. Typically to handle HA a RabbitMQ "
"cluster should be placed between a load balancer and the front-end "
"application server to handle cross host connections. The ports necessary "
"to forward in a Rabbit MQ cluster are (5672, and 61613). A RabbitMQ "
"cluster can run on smaller memory machines depending on how frequent "
"large requests bursts occur. 4 - 8 GB of Memory is recommended to start."
msgstr ""
"The Messaging tier is an AMQP based tier along con STOMP Protocol (used "
"for agent communication). The primary model recommended is para usar "
"RabbitMQ for queue services. RabbitMQ is también a cluster-based queuing "
"system y needs al menos 3 instances for HA configurations. This is due to"
" elections in the failover scenarios RabbitMQ can manage. If doing a "
"cross-region HA RabbitMQ cluster, se recomienda have al menos 3 Rabbit "
"queue clusters per region. Typically to handle HA a RabbitMQ cluster "
"debería ser placed entre a load balancer y the front-end application "
"server to handle cross host connections. The ports necessary to forward "
"in a Rabbit MQ cluster are (5672, y 61613). A RabbitMQ cluster can run on"
" smaller memory machines dependiendo de how frequent large requests "
"bursts occur. 4 - 8 GB of Memory se recomienda para iniciar."

